# All text files are normalized to LF in the repo AND forced to LF on checkout.
# `eol=lf` (not bare `text`) is required so that a Windows checkout performed
# with the default core.autocrlf=true still produces LF working-tree bytes.
# This matters because Study/02 byte-hashes frozen artifacts whose approved
# SHA-256 is computed over LF content:
#   configs/A-g2-protocol-v1.json, configs/A-g2-search-v1.json,
#   configs/A-g3-pilot-amendment-v4.json,
#   artifacts/pilot/G3-matrix/experiment_matrix.csv
# Under bare `text`, autocrlf=true would smudge those to CRLF on checkout and
# break verify_frozen_hashes / FROZEN_MATRIX_SHA256. With eol=lf the working
# tree matches the approved bytes with no manual git config or file rewriting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.css   text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
src/data/method-status.generated.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

*.docx binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pt   binary
*.pth  binary

